  "presentation_summary": [
    "27-year-old woman with 4 months of intermittent fever and 3.5 months of fatigue and dark urine was initially treated as drug-induced liver injury.",
    "At admission she remained febrile to 39.5 C and had marked hepatitis, low fibrinogen, elevated LDH, mild thrombocytopenia, low CRP, and negative TB/fungal/bacterial culture workup.",
    "During the course she developed rising EBV DNA, EBER-positive liver tissue, abnormal NK-cell population in marrow, hematochezia, hypofibrinogenemia, ferritin >1200, sCD25 20312 pg/mL, hemophagocytosis, and fatal GI hemorrhage/multiorgan failure.",
    "EBV DNA, EBER liver pathology, marrow flow cytometry, and hemophagocytosis are stored outside ordinary observations."
  ],
